# Template for the repository .env -- copy to .env and fill in.
#
#   copy .env.example .env
#
# .env is git-ignored; this file is not, and must never contain a real key.
# tools/env.js loads .env at require time for every tool that talks to PubMed or
# OpenAlex, so nothing has to be typed on a command line -- a flag would put a
# live secret into shell history and into the terminal scrollback of a recorded
# session.
#
# A value already set in the real environment wins over the file, so a one-off
# override or CI secret still works.
#
# An OpenAlex key is effectively required in practice: the anonymous pool
# returned HTTP 429 with Retry-After 44969s (~12.5h) on 2026-11-03, which stops
# a corroboration sweep. With a key the same request returns HTTP 200. Get one
# free at https://openalex.org/settings.

OPENALEX_API_KEY=
NCBI_API_KEY=
CROSSCHECK_EMAIL=
